<title>USA: Philadelphia, Baltimore papers win prizes.</title>
<headline>Philadelphia, Baltimore papers win prizes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>A reporter and two photographers of The Philadelphia Inquirer -- Michael Vitez, April Saul and Ron Cortes -- won the Pulitzer Prize for explanatory journalism on Monday for a series on the choices that confronted critically-ill patients seeking to die with dignity.</p>
<p>The Pulitzer Prize for feature writing was awarded to Lisa Pollak of The Baltimore Sun. The Pulitzer board cited her &quot;compelling portrait of a baseball umpire who endured the death of a son while knowing that another son suffers from the same deadly genetic disease.&quot;</p>
</text>
